Bugfix: Let the tab order of the header follow the document

The layout of every signed-in page assigned six positive tabindex values, to
the skip link, the logo, the app menu, the app navigation, the search box and
the user menu. A positive value pulls its element in front of every element
with tabindex="0", so these six came before the whole page content, in an
order that had to be kept by hand. The burger of the app menu was a button
nested inside a link and therefore a seventh stop, which the browser placed
after all six - the focus left the header at its right edge and jumped back
to a control at its left.

The values are gone and the tab order follows the document. The skip link
remains the first stop of the page through its position alone. The user menu
keeps tabindex="0", because it is a div and not focusable without it. The
burger is a span and no longer a control of its own, which also removed a
nested control from the markup.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.3, SC 4.1.2
